  "question": {
    "text": "Among the triatomic molecules/ions, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> , the total number of linear molecule(s)/ion(s) where the hybridization of the central atom does not have contribution from the d-orbital(s) is<br />[Atomic number: S = 16, Cl = 17, I = 53 and Xe = 54]",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BeCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8203;</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#8203;</mo></math>&nbsp;is the linear molecule where&nbsp;the hybridization of the central atom does not have contribution from the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>-</mo></math>orbital.&nbsp;</p><p>In the remaining molecules/ions,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> ​&nbsp;is bent,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>​&nbsp;is V shaped with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo></math>hybridization,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><msub><mi>ICl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8722;</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>​,&nbsp;are linear with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math>&nbsp;hybridization.</p>",
